            <ArticleTitle>Monkeys overharvest shellfish.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.7554/eLife.30865</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">e30865</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The use of stone tools by macaques in Thailand has reduced the size and population density of coastal shellfish: previously it was thought that overharvesting effects resulted from human activity alone.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
